# Measuring what a camera actually does. Two stages that want opposite
# fields, which is why the words matter: asking for both at once gets one
# of them silently wrong.

msgid "profile.title"
msgstr "Measure this camera"

msgid "profile.heading"
msgstr "Measure this camera"

#. Says what it buys, because a calibration nobody understands is a
#. calibration nobody runs.
msgid "profile.body"
msgstr ""
"Two short measurements, once per camera. They tell darlaston how much "
"slide each resolution really shows, and how this camera's exposure "
"control maps to brightness. Both are things cameras differ on and "
"neither can be worked out from the numbers a camera reports."

#. Stage one. Needs detail: matching has nothing to work with otherwise.
msgid "profile.stage.geometry"
msgstr ""
"1. Field of view.  Put a slide in and focus it, or close the field "
"diaphragm down so there is a sharp edge in view. This needs detail to "
"measure against, and will say so rather than guess if it cannot see any."

#. Stage two. Needs the opposite.
msgid "profile.stage.response"
msgstr ""
"2. Exposure response.  Now defocus, so the field is even. This one "
"measures brightness, so anything with structure in it would be "
"measuring the specimen instead of the camera."

msgid "profile.action.geometry"
msgstr "Measure field of view"

msgid "profile.action.response"
msgstr "Measure exposure"

msgid "profile.action.close"
msgstr "Done"

msgid "profile.measuring"
msgstr "measuring {what}…"

msgid "profile.geometry.done"
msgstr "Measured {n} of {total} resolution modes."

#. Not a failure of the camera. Almost always an unlit scope.
msgid "profile.geometry.nothing"
msgstr ""
"Nothing to measure against. The field looks blank, so the lamp may be "
"off or the light path blocked. Put something with detail in view and "
"try again."

msgid "profile.response.done"
msgstr ""
"Exposure behaves predictably from {low} to {high} ({n} of {total} steps "
"measured)."

msgid "profile.response.nothing"
msgstr ""
"The brightness barely changed across the sweep. Check the lamp is on "
"and the exposure is not already clipping."

msgid "profile.failed"
msgstr "Could not finish: {why}"

#. This camera has no way to be measured; a vendor SDK camera reports its
#. own numbers and does not need it.
msgid "profile.unavailable"
msgstr "This camera does not support measuring."

msgid "setup.cameras.action.profile"
msgstr "Measure…"

msgid "setup.cameras.profile.tooltip"
msgstr ""
"Measure what this camera really does: how much slide each resolution "
"shows, and how its exposure control maps to brightness. Once per camera."
